EV6 patch 8851-0003: surprise unplug guards (reduced port of the 88x2bu build's patch 0003)

Why: on the car an unplug while the interface is up can hang or crash the kernel, and the
  head unit's kernel panics on soft lockups, so the head unit reboots.
What:
  - rtw_dev_remove(): if the usb core already marked the device NOTATTACHED (unplug), set
    surprise-removed before the netdevs are unregistered.
  - usbctrl_vendorreq(): stop retrying once the device cannot do I/O any more.
Not ported (the G6/PHL driver is structured differently): the tasklet and cfg80211
  call guards of the 88x2bu patch. EXPERIMENTAL: not tested with the real dongle.

diff --git a/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c b/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c
index 19d8211..97238f7 100755
--- a/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c
@@ -1042,6 +1042,15 @@ static void rtw_dev_remove(struct usb_interface *pusb_intf)
 		rtw_usbfs_unhide(pusb_intf);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * EV6: on an unplug the usb core has already marked the device NOTATTACHED. Mark it
+	 * removed now, before the netdevs are unregistered, so that ndo_stop and cfg80211's
+	 * stop_ap/disconnect paths do not send register I/O and commands (with retries and
+	 * waits) to a device that is gone. The car's kernel panics on soft lockups.
+	 */
+	if (interface_to_usbdev(pusb_intf)->state == USB_STATE_NOTATTACHED)
+		dev_set_surprise_removed(dvobj);
+
 	dvobj->processing_dev_remove = _TRUE;
 
 	/* TODO: use rtw_os_ndevs_deinit instead at the first stage of driver's dev deinit function */
diff --git a/os_dep/linux/usb_ops_linux.c b/os_dep/linux/usb_ops_linux.c
index 3f57597..11b64c4 100755
--- a/os_dep/linux/usb_ops_linux.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/usb_ops_linux.c
@@ -138,6 +138,9 @@ int usbctrl_vendorreq(struct dvobj_priv *pdvobjpriv, u8 request, u16 value, u16
 				dev_set_surprise_removed(pdvobjpriv);
 				break;
 			}
+			/* EV6: no more retries once the device is known to be gone (unplug) */
+			if (RTW_CANNOT_IO(pdvobjpriv))
+				break;
 
 		}
 
